From 17a97e50d5535f0033b8d4aa0f57bb8b9d0a54c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Mittell <mittell@me.com>
Date: Sun, 29 Mar 2026 11:29:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): sync env-var-backed token credentials into agent
 auth store
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When openclaw.json declares auth profiles with mode 'token' (e.g.
anthropic:me.com), the actual bearer token may live in an env var
loaded from credentials/*.env. The gateway's main session picks this
up at boot, but the per-agent auth-profiles.json can go stale after
a token refresh — causing all embedded runner sessions (sub-agents,
scheduler jobs, compaction) to fail with FailoverError timeout while
the main session works fine.

Extend syncExternalCliCredentials to also resolve env-var-backed token
credentials on every store load. The env var name is derived from the
profile id: 'anthropic:me.com' -> ANTHROPIC_ME_COM_TOKEN.

This ensures the embedded runner always sees the current token without
requiring external sync scripts or manual intervention.

Fixes: embedded sessions timing out after OAuth token refresh
